WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.362
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:09.211
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:15.100
Unit fifteen: Entertainment. Today you will tell what was happening with the past continuous.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.308
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.546
Streaming service.

7
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.697
Streaming service means a website or app for watching shows online.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.817
We watch movies on a streaming service.

9
00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:36.673
Your turn. Say: Streaming service.

10
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.813
Streaming service.

11
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.516
Episode.

12
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:46.097
Episode means one part of a TV series.

13
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.066
I watched three episodes last night.

14
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.256
Your turn. Say: Episode.

15
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.031
Episode.

16
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:57.784
Series.

17
00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:01.596
Series means a TV show with many episodes.

18
00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:04.160
This series has five seasons.

19
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.472
Your turn. Say: Series.

20
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:11.404
Series.

21
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.244
Plot twist.

22
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.935
Plot twist means a sudden surprise in a story.

23
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.550
The plot twist shocked everyone!

24
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.826
Your turn. Say: Plot twist.

25
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.749
Plot twist.

26
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:28.426
Cliffhanger.

27
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:32.508
Cliffhanger means an exciting ending that makes you want more.

28
00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:35.081
The episode ended on a cliffhanger.

29
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:38.022
Your turn. Say: Cliffhanger.

30
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.019
Cliffhanger.

31
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:44.295
Binge-watch.

32
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:48.630
Binge-watch means to watch many episodes at one time.

33
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:51.123
We binge-watched the whole season.

34
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:54.311
Your turn. Say: Binge-watch.

35
00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.354
Binge-watch.

36
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:00.245
Celebrity.

37
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.400
Celebrity means a famous person.

38
00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:06.016
A celebrity visited our city.

39
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:09.141
Your turn. Say: Celebrity.

40
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.071
Celebrity.

41
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:14.829
Award show.

42
00:02:15.817 --> 00:02:18.768
Award show means a TV event where prizes are given.

43
00:02:19.383 --> 00:02:20.872
She won at the award show.

44
00:02:21.483 --> 00:02:24.043
Your turn. Say: Award show.

45
00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.133
Award show.

46
00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:30.012
Fanbase.

47
00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.864
Fanbase means all the fans of someone or something.

48
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.415
The band has a huge fanbase.

49
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:39.901
Your turn. Say: Fanbase.

50
00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:43.872
Fanbase.

51
00:02:44.617 --> 00:02:45.293
Review.

52
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:49.618
Review means an opinion about a film, book or show.

53
00:02:50.217 --> 00:02:52.019
The movie got good reviews.

54
00:02:52.617 --> 00:02:55.362
Your turn. Say: Review.

55
00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.155
Review.

56
00:02:59.917 --> 00:03:00.662
Rating.

57
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.660
Rating means a score that shows how good something is.

58
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.400
It has a rating of nine out of ten.

59
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:10.495
Your turn. Say: Rating.

60
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.207
Rating.

61
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.218
Recommendation.

62
00:03:17.217 --> 00:03:20.366
Recommendation means a suggestion of something good.

63
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.683
Thanks for the recommendation!

64
00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:26.238
Your turn. Say: Recommendation.

65
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.438
Recommendation.

66
00:03:31.233 --> 00:03:35.267
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:36.117 --> 00:03:38.070
Visal, you look tired today!

68
00:03:39.183 --> 00:03:43.984
I binge-watched a series last night. I was watching until midnight!

69
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:45.945
Was it good?

70
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:51.223
Amazing! I was eating noodles when the big plot twist happened.

71
00:03:52.317 --> 00:03:53.550
Do you recommend it?

72
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.917
Yes! It has a high rating. But every episode ends on a cliffhanger!

73
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.683
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.934
Grammar focus: Past continuous.

75
00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:07.491
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:10.810
I was watching the show when the plot twist happened.

77
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.763
They were talking about the celebrity.

78
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.510
What were you doing at nine o'clock?

79
00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:23.625
Use the past continuous for a longer action. Use the past simple for the short action that interrupts it.

80
00:04:24.383 --> 00:04:28.824
Be careful! Don't say: I watched the show when the plot twist happened.

81
00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:33.892
Say: I was watching the show when the plot twist happened.

82
00:04:34.192 --> 00:04:36.993
Use the past continuous for the longer action.

83
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.557
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.728
One More Episode.

85
00:04:43.028 --> 00:04:47.547
Last weekend, I binge-watched a whole series on a streaming service.

86
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:51.427
I was eating dinner when the biggest plot twist happened.

87
00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:56.047
Every episode ended with a cliffhanger, so I couldn't stop.

88
00:04:57.033 --> 00:05:00.310
The fanbase gave the show a high rating and great reviews.

89
00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:05.204
It won three prizes at an award show, so it's my top recommendation.

90
00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.186
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.317
I blank watching TV when you called.

92
00:05:13.617 --> 00:05:16.550
A, was. B, were. C, am.

93
00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.786
The answer is A: was.

94
00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.426
A sudden surprise in a story is a blank.

95
00:05:25.726 --> 00:05:29.321
A, plot twist. B, rating. C, fanbase.

96
00:05:32.867 --> 00:05:34.866
The answer is A: plot twist.

97
00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:38.957
To watch many episodes at one time is to blank.

98
00:05:39.257 --> 00:05:43.015
A, binge-watch. B, review. C, stream.

99
00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.845
The answer is A: binge-watch.

100
00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:53.057
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:53.917 --> 00:05:57.182
Recommend a TV series or movie and explain the plot.

102
00:06:05.983 --> 00:06:07.542
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:07.842 --> 00:06:16.882
I recommend a series about a young chef. She was working in a small kitchen when a famous judge tasted her food. The plot twists are great!

104
00:06:17.182 --> 00:06:18.799
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:19.683 --> 00:06:23.996
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and past continuous.

106
00:06:24.296 --> 00:06:29.189
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

107
00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:32.211
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:32.511 --> 00:06:34.966
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

